      "message": "i think you can cut down on some of the unsafe (e.g. in the drop impl and the explicit `cookie_incr_refcount` in `new`) if you do something like this\n\n```\npub struct Accessor\u003cF: Fn() -\u003e Option\u003cConnectionInfo\u003e + Send + Sync + \u0027static\u003e {\n    accessor: *mut sys::ARpc_Accessor,\n    callback: Arc\u003cF\u003e,\n}\n```\n\nif we don\u0027t want to make `Accessor` generic, you could do something like `callback: Box\u003cdyn Drop\u003e` to erase the type (needs an extra alloc though) or use `Arc\u003cdyn Fn() -\u003e Option\u003cConnectionInfo\u003e + Send + Sync + \u0027static\u003e` throughout (which is basically the rust equiv of `std::function\u003c...\u003e`)",
